{
  "name": "always_order_after_reentry",
  "description": "XState keeps the previous snapshot (and so the previous order of its state nodes) when a microstep leaves the configuration and the history value unchanged. Re-entering s, which owns a history node, records history and so moves s1 behind t1; re-entering t (no history node) changes nothing, so t1 stays ahead of s1. When ARM enables both conflicting always transitions, t1's is selected first and wins (y). After BACK re-enters p in document order, ARM lets s1's win (x).",
  "tags": [
    "always",
    "parallel",
    "conflict",
    "history",
    "reenter",
    "selection"
  ],
